Z||000003||Jefrysuko||05-24-2001||04:00 AM||||There is something wrong with those wheels.  Alot of gap between them and the fenders.  The front one isn't centered either!  Or is it just to early in the morning?<P>------------------<BR>Jeffrey D Suckow<BR>88 GT<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:Jefrysuko@aol.com">Jefrysuko@aol.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||05-24-2001||10:38 AM||||1)-That was VERY early in the morning when you posted that!<P>2)-The steering was turned slightly, making the front look a little off.  It's not, really, trust me.  I am, but the wheel's not.<P>3)-The fender gap is caused by:<BR>....(a)-The car has not been lowered, so there is, in fact, a gap (do you think I could get into a lowered Fiero?); and<BR>....(b)-The camera was no higher than my eye level, maybe even lower, so you're looking right up into my *gasp* exposed wheelwells, (you Perv).<P>Geez, it's just a sig-pic, and this was just a test-topic.  Everybody's a critic!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||05:51 PM||||Looks good!  I wouldnt say that you have too much wheel well gap.  I've got 14" rims with P195/70R14 tires on it, and it looks about the same as yours.  Maybe it is because my tires have more sidewall than yours?<P>Either way, it's still a good sig pic!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
